+ * Derived from libavcodec/mips/cabac.h (Loongson/Imagination, LGPL 2.1+)
+ * with the following changes for the PSP:
+ *   - the bytestream is read with two lbu instead of lhu: the CABAC data
+ *     starts at an arbitrary byte offset and the Allegrex traps on
+ *     unaligned halfword loads (no kernel fix-up on the PSP);
+ *   - explicit .set noreorder with hand-filled delay slots (psp-gcc
+ *     assembles inline asm in reorder mode, which pads every branch with
+ *     a nop);
+ *   - LPS/MPS selection is branchless (mask form of the C reference), the
+ *     Allegrex has no branch predictor so a fixed-cost path is preferred;
+ *   - refill and the renormalisation shift use clz (Allegrex has it) instead
+ *     of the norm_shift table: one dependent load less per bin (3.5 cycles
+ *     load-use on the hardware).
+ *
+ * Bit-exactness against the C reference is checked by the swdec harness
+ * (per-frame CRC against a host golden).
